    "section": "Dominatus Event Companion",
    "order": 180,
    "anchor": "win-path-2",
    "summary": "Win path means when a player’s wins and losses came, not how many. Pairing by it tends to match strength of schedule, but mainly makes games more enjoyable, since opponents share a recent experience.\n\nFor example, two players at 3–1:\n\n- One lost game 1, then won 3 in a row, and is likely in high spirits.\n- The other started 3–0, then lost game 4: a sharp letdown.\n\nPaired together, they would be in very different moods.",
